  "definition": "Supply chain finance (SCF) is the use of financing and risk mitigation practices and techniques to optimise the management of the working capital and liquidity invested in supply chain processes and transactions.[^1] The Standard Definitions for Techniques of Supply Chain Finance add that SCF is typically applied to open account trade and is triggered by supply chain events, and that visibility of the underlying trade flows by the finance provider is a necessary component, which can be enabled by a technology platform.[^1]",
